{
  "id": "is-graph-bipartite",
  "questionId": "is-graph-bipartite",
  "slug": "is-graph-bipartite",
  "title": "Is Graph Bipartite",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Graphs",
  "patterns": [
    "graph dfs/bfs",
    "coloring",
    "adjacency list"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "bipartite means you can color every node with one of two colors so no edge connects two same-colored nodes",
    "run BFS or DFS from any unvisited node, assigning it a color, then assign every neighbor the opposite color",
    "if you ever reach a neighbor that already has a color, and it matches the current node's color, the graph is not bipartite",
    "remember to check every connected component separately, since a disconnected graph can have several"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "only checking one connected component and missing that others might contain an odd cycle",
    "not detecting a conflict when a neighbor was already colored the same as the current node",
    "assuming a graph with no cycles at all needs checking - trees are always bipartite, but you still must run the coloring correctly"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an undirected graph with n nodes labeled 0 to n-1, described\nby an adjacency list `graph` where `graph[i]` is the list of nodes\nadjacent to node i (there are no self loops or repeated edges). A graph\nis bipartite if its nodes can be split into two groups such that every\nedge connects a node in one group to a node in the other group (no edge\nstays within a group).\n\n**Return true if the graph is bipartite.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= n <= 100",
      "0 <= graph[i][j] <= n - 1",
      "graph[i] does not contain i and has no duplicate entries"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "graph with no edges",
      "graph containing an odd-length cycle (not bipartite)",
      "graph containing only even-length cycles (bipartite)",
      "disconnected graph where one component is bipartite and you must still check all components"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "graph = [[1,3],[0,2],[1,3],[0,2]]",
        "output": "true",
        "expectedOutput": "true",
        "explanation": "nodes {0,2} can go in one group and {1,3} in the other, every edge crosses groups"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "graph = [[1,2,3],[0,2],[0,1,3],[0,2]]",
        "output": "false",
        "expectedOutput": "false",
        "explanation": "0-1-2-0 forms a triangle (odd cycle), which can never be 2-colored"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
